			"Message": "feat(Output): Separate system and user extension scanning in IPC shim\n\nThe ExtensionScannerIPC transform plugin now distinguishes between system and user extensions by calling the appropriate Mountain IPC methods:\n- `extensions:scanSystemExtensions` for built-in extensions (ForceBuiltin=true)\n- `extensions:scanUserExtensions` for user-installed extensions (ForceBuiltin=false)\n\nPreviously the scanner hardcoded `type: 0` and `isBuiltin: true` for all extensions, causing all extensions to appear under @builtin in the sidebar. Now it honours Mountain's ILocalExtension envelope values (type, isBuiltin, source) with ForceBuiltin as fallback for older envelopes.\n\nAlso implements the previously stubbed `scanUserExtensions()` method which was returning an empty array, and makes `scanAllUserExtensions()` delegate to it.",
			"SHA": "a7b92b8faec7cf334dc5f572fd889561f4703166"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T00:28:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				215,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Fix regex for minified code and correct userDataSync channel name\n\nTwo fixes for the Output build pipeline:\n\n1. CatchOutputFolderRejection regex now matches both `() => undefined` and `() => void 0` (the minified form esbuild produces). The appended catch handler also uses `void 0` for consistency with minified output.\n\n2. TauriMainProcessService channel stub keys corrected: `userDataSyncService` → `userDataSync` and `userDataSync` → `userDataSyncAccount`. VS Code registers the channel as `userDataSync` (not `userDataSyncService`), so the stub was unreachable causing sync to fail silently.\n\nRefs: The channel name discovery was confirmed by grepping the VS Code source at `workbench/services/userDataSync/electron-browser/userDataSyncService.ts:13`.",
			"SHA": "bf9bfcd67bfb89f90fac75177e7465d81f209b0e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T00:02:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				215,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Fix binary file corruption in FileProtocolShim\n\nThe file:read Tauri command was incorrectly invoked with named-object\nargs ({ path, encoding: \"utf8\" }) and the response was assumed to be\na string. Mountain actually returns raw bytes as { buffer: number[] } and\nignores the encoding param entirely.\n\nWhen VS Code loaded binary files (WASM, fonts, images), the response\nbody became \"[object Object]\" which corrupted the data. This broke\nTextMate syntax highlighting with:\n  \"WebAssembly.Module doesn't parse at byte 0: module doesn't start\n   with '\\0asm'\"\n\nFix by:\n1. Invoking file:read with positional array args [path] as expected\n   by MountainIPCInvoke\n2. Adding UnwrapReadResult() to unwrap { buffer: number[] } into\n   Uint8Array for binary-safe Response bodies\n3. Updating content type to Uint8Array | string | Blob | null\n\nAll three protocol handlers (VSCodeFileHandler, VSCodeUserDataHandler,\nFileHandler) now use the binary-safe pattern.",
			"SHA": "2f14553fa6611e381918643364ca6e0c65155a9c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:44:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				215,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add CatchOutputFolderRejection transform plugin\n\nAdd Step 15 to the build pipeline that catches an unhandled promise rejection\nfrom VS Code's outputServices.createFolder(). In Land, the VFS-IPC stat call\nrejects with FileNotFound before fileService can swallow it, causing the\nrejection to propagate past the .then(() => undefined) handler and surface as\ntelemetry noise in PostHog.\n\nThe plugin uses a regex match against outputServices.js to append\n.catch(() => undefined) to the createFolder chain, silencing the harmless\nrejection since the output folder is created lazily on first channel write\nanyway. If upstream VS Code changes the exact .then(() => undefined) shape,\nthe Match() returns Unchanged and a LOG line surfaces as a regression tripwire.",
			"SHA": "a900f339a30600bc403059043a5a71f9a2b4c854"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:24:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				212,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add IPC stubs for extension tips, MCP, sync, and language detection\n\nAdd missing stub handlers to TauriMainProcessService to prevent renderer crashes when VS Code code calls these services without Mountain handlers:\n\n- IExtensionTipsService: exeBasedRecommendations.ts calls .forEach() on the result, requiring array stubs (empty = no recommendations)\n- IMcpManagementService / IMcpWorkbenchManagement: mcpManagementIpc.ts calls .map() on server arrays, requiring array stubs\n- IUserDataSyncService: userDataSyncServiceIpc.ts destructures a [status, conflicts, lastSyncTime] tuple, requiring tuple stub\n- ILanguageDetectionService: iterates fileExtensions.extensions, requiring object stub with nested empty extensions array\n\nThese stubs return safe empty values that VS Code's workbench code can gracefully handle, preventing TypeError crashes in the renderer.",
			"SHA": "1452db402083b54d42dd76a6ab8ea6a45111f087"
		}
	],
